menu "C5VRX"

config C5VRX_LINK_MODE
    bool "Link mode: no DAC output, BitScrambler in loopback for host dumps"
    default n
    help
        Build the receiver without the PARLIO TX / resistor DAC path. The
        single BitScrambler of the ESP32-C5 is then free for loopback runs
        of the same Phase5 FM demodulator over snapshots of the raw I/Q
        ring, and the console 'v' key dumps one snapshot plus its
        demodulated CVBS as hex for tools/link_dump.py. This is the first
        step of the T-Embed display link (frames over UART instead of an
        analog output). The OSD menu is unavailable in this mode.

config C5VRX_LINK_CHANNEL
    int "Link mode: FPV channel at boot (band x 8 + channel - 1)"
    depends on C5VRX_LINK_MODE
    range 0 47
    default 5
    help
        Index into the receiver's channel table: bands R, A, B, E, F, L in
        that order, 8 channels each. 5 = R6 (5843 MHz), 8 = A1 (5865 MHz).
        Link mode also forces the wide (BW40) analog filter.

config C5VRX_LINK_STREAM
    bool "Link mode: stream frames over UART from boot"
    depends on C5VRX_LINK_MODE
    default y
    help
        Grab frames continuously and send them to a display board (LilyGo
        T-Embed) over UART, protocol in main/link_proto.h. Console keys:
        'S' streaming on/off, 'P' picture mode, 'N' channel scan, 'M'
        horizontal smoothing.

config C5VRX_LINK_DEBUG
    bool "Link mode: debug output and dump tools"
    depends on C5VRX_LINK_MODE
    default n
    help
        Adds what is only needed at the desk: the [STREAM] statistics line
        every second and [LOST] traces, the receiver's AGC status lines, and
        the console dumps 'v' (raw I/Q plus BitScrambler loopback
        demodulation, tools/link_dump.py) and 'g' (one frame,
        tools/link_frame.py). Off in the final build: nothing is printed
        while streaming, and the loopback BitScrambler and its 24 KB of DMA
        buffers are not set up. PlatformIO environment xiao_c5_link_debug
        turns it on.

config C5VRX_LINK_PICTURE_MODE
    int "Link mode: picture mode at boot (0 auto, 1 fine, 2 raw)"
    depends on C5VRX_LINK_MODE
    range 0 2
    default 0
    help
        0 auto: rows coded near-losslessly, the tolerance chosen per frame so
        that a frame fits the link in the time the grabber needs for it (up
        to 25 fps PAL at 4 Mbaud). 1 fine: tolerance +/- 1 level, fewer fps.
        2 raw: 8-bit rows, about 10 fps at 4 Mbaud. The display board can
        switch modes at run time.

config C5VRX_LINK_UART_TX_GPIO
    int "Link mode: UART TX GPIO"
    depends on C5VRX_LINK_MODE
    default 11
    help
        11 is XIAO pad D6. Connect it to the display board's RX (T-Embed
        UART connector RXD, GPIO44).

config C5VRX_LINK_UART_RX_GPIO
    int "Link mode: UART RX GPIO"
    depends on C5VRX_LINK_MODE
    default 12
    help
        12 is XIAO pad D7 (display board TX, T-Embed GPIO43): commands from
        the display (scan, channel steps, picture mode).

config C5VRX_LINK_UART_BAUD
    int "Link mode: UART baud rate"
    depends on C5VRX_LINK_MODE
    default 4000000
    help
        4000000 is proven on the bench. 5000000 is the limit of both UARTs
        (ESP32-C5 and ESP32-S3) and gives the auto picture mode 25 % more
        bytes per frame; the display firmware follows either rate.

endmenu
